From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Norman Herms <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 07:39:26 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: allwinner: a733-cubie-a7s: describe ALDO1 as
 VCC-PL

ALDO1 of the PMIC supplies the pin banks PL and PG and the EEPROM
(schematic V1.10 p.4, p.7, p.16), but the board device tree does not
describe it. Bank PG is the supply of the TWI0 pull-ups R97 and R98
(2.2 kOhm, VCC-PG tied to VCC-PL through RA3, schematic V1.10 p.7) and
has no supply property yet.

Add ALDO1 as a fixed 3.3 V regulator named vcc-pl and set it as the
bank PG supply of the pin controller. The voltage is read back from the
PMIC (ALDO1 enabled, 3.3 V). It stays on: it feeds bank PL, and the PMIC
sits on the bus of that bank.

r_pio gets no vcc-pl-supply. The PMIC is on r_i2c0 on PL0 and PL1. The
pin driver requests the supply of a bank when a device takes pins of that
bank, so a supply from ALDO1 would defer r_i2c0 for ever and the PMIC
that provides ALDO1 would never probe. The bank PG supply does not write
a register: the A733 pin controller has no io_bias variant, so the driver
only gets and enables the regulator.

Not covered: the PMIC input AIN234, which ALDO1 feeds, stays undescribed
as before.

Tested on Radxa Cubie A7S: the PMIC probes without a bank PL supply, and
bank PG takes ALDO1 as its supply.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 .../dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s.dts     | 17 +++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s.dts
index 61ecb941a82a..d7acd2fee254 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s.dts
@@ -334,6 +334,7 @@ &pio {
 	vcc-pb-supply = <&reg_swout2>;
 	vcc-pc-supply = <&reg_cldo5>;
 	vcc-pd-supply = <&reg_swout1>;
+	vcc-pg-supply = <&reg_aldo1>;
 	vcc-ph-supply = <&reg_swout2>;
 };
 
@@ -363,6 +364,22 @@ axp318: pmic@36 {
 		dldoin-supply = <&reg_vcc5v0_sys>;
 
 		regulators {
+			/*
+			 * VCC-PL: bank PL (the PMIC bus pins), bank PG, the
+			 * EEPROM and the TWI0 pull-ups. Always on: the PMIC bus
+			 * runs on bank PL. Bank PL has no vcc-pl-supply on
+			 * r_pio: the PMIC sits on r_i2c0 (PL0/PL1), and the pin
+			 * driver requests the bank supply when r_i2c0 gets its
+			 * pins, so the supply of ALDO1 would defer the pins
+			 * and the PMIC that provides ALDO1 would never probe.
+			 */
+			reg_aldo1: aldo1 {
+				regulator-name = "vcc-pl";
+				regulator-min-microvolt = <3300000>;
+				regulator-max-microvolt = <3300000>;
+				regulator-always-on;
+			};
+
 			reg_dcdc1: dcdc1 {
 				regulator-name = "vcc-3v3-sys";
 				regulator-min-microvolt = <3300000>;
